------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Defensive publication / prior art
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
This project is released as a defensive disclosure. Its concepts and
implementation are hereby placed in the public record as prior art, in
particular:

  - an MCP server exposing a curated catalogue of natural-language and poetic
    "thinking patterns" classified by a closed set of cognitive axes;
  - retrieval of those patterns by problem theme, with exclusion of the user's
    own input language so that structurally contrasting lenses are surfaced
    (the `exclude_names` contrast mechanism);
  - the method of automatically analyzing the grammatical bias of an input
    natural-language text, mapping that bias to a closed set of cognitive axes,
    and selecting one or more structurally orthogonal patterns (a different
    natural language or a bound poetic/formal structure) from such a catalogue —
    excluding the input language — in order to reframe the text and expose
    assumptions that are artifacts of the source grammar rather than inherent to
    the subject; this selection and reframing performed either automatically by
    a software agent or interactively (both embodiments are disclosed); and
  - the method of reframing a problem through such a contrasting language or
    form (see README.md and .claude/skills/reframe-through-structure).

The intent is defensive: by disclosing these techniques publicly and with a
verifiable date, they cannot later be validly patented by a third party and
asserted against the users of this software. Effectiveness as prior art depends
on public, timestamped availability; the authoritative date is this
repository's public version-control history together with any tagged or
archived release.

